    '=== PART 1 ===',
    'TITLE: The Quiet Architecture of Acoustic Design',
    'Most people judge a public building by its facade, natural light, or spatial layout, yet the way a room handles sound largely {{1|A:slips|B:goes|C:runs|D:falls|ANS:B|EXP:Fixed C1 collocation "go unnoticed" meaning to remain overlooked.|WA:"Slip" needs a particle such as "slip by" or "slip through", not a bare adjective.|WC:"Run" does not collocate with "unnoticed" (compare "run wild" or "run dry").|WD:"Fall" collocates with "silent" or "short", not "unnoticed".}} unnoticed until something goes wrong. Modern acoustic engineering {{2|A:extends|B:stretches|C:reaches|D:spans|ANS:A|EXP:"Extend beyond" is the standard formal collocation for abstract scope or application.|WB:"Stretch" usually describes physical length or limits (e.g., "stretch a budget").|WC:"Reach" typically takes a concrete endpoint rather than abstract "far beyond".|WD:"Span" is transitive and takes a direct object without "beyond" (e.g., "spans three decades").}} far beyond symphony halls and recording studios; it shapes hospitals, classrooms, and open-plan offices alike. Studies consistently show that poorly controlled background noise can {{3|A:exert|B:impose|C:inflict|D:enforce|ANS:A|EXP:Strong C1 verb-noun collocation: "exert an influence on".|WB:"Impose" collocates with rules, limits, or penalties, not "influence".|WC:"Inflict" collocates with harm, pain, or damage, not neutral "influence".|WD:"Enforce" applies to laws, rules, or standards, not "influence".}} a measurable influence on cognitive stamina, subtly raising stress hormones even when occupants believe they have tuned it out.',
