    'Sceptics occasionally dismiss this turn towards typological research as timid nostalgia, arguing that urgent climate and housing crises call for radical technological disruption rather than backward glances. Yet that objection rests on a false dichotomy. Studying how earlier builders handled monsoon rain or dense communal living does not preclude using computational modelling or low-carbon engineered timber; on the contrary, combining ancestral spatial intelligence with modern fabrication often yields solutions far more resilient than futuristic prototypes invented in a vacuum.',
    '',
